                    "patching_rect": [ 409.0, 48.0, 476.0, 75.0 ],
                    "text": "I find it handy to be able to use external params when writing code, but we also may wish to drive the frequency of an LFO externally. This logic checks to see if there is an external signal driver (greater than 0, but also checking to see if the last signal was also zero, to account for resets). If it is zero for two samples or longer, switch to external param"
